{
  "story": "This simplified diploid animal cell has two homologous pairs; DNA replication is complete, and segregation is error-free. Follow the labeled chromosomes from condensation to two nuclei. Compare each daughter set with the starting reference to see what mitosis preserves. Use Previous and Next; every state waits for you.",
  "aha": {
    "stateId": "telophase",
    "observation": "Mitosis separates sister chromatids into two nuclei, each preserving the starting chromosome number and identities."
  },
  "layout": {
    "preset": "stepper-states-cycle",
    "width": 640
  },
  "parts": [
    {
      "id": "stage-rail",
      "kind": "step-rail",
      "presentation": "Use the approved card shell, with story and instructions above the experiment. Keep stage progression on this rail, not inside the picture.",
      "bind": {
        "active": "inputs.stage",
        "items": "variant.states"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mitosis-picture",
      "kind": "fixed-picture",
      "presentation": "Use the canonical mitosis cycle arrangement and shared scale throughout. Region phases correspond positionally to variant.states. Keep the starting reference distinct from the experimental cell. A/B identify homologous pairs; superscripts m/p identify maternal/paternal chromosomes. Keep chromosome labels visible; phase descriptions specify picture states, not additional captions.",
      "bind": {
        "active": "state.active",
        "links": "variant.links",
        "regions": "variant.regions"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "active-part",
      "kind": "active-callout",
      "presentation": "Anchor beside the selected region without covering chromosomes. Identify the mechanism here; reserve numerical measurements for the readouts.",
      "bind": {
        "target": "state.calloutRegion",
        "text": "state.sentence",
        "reason": "state.why"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "chromosome-evidence",
      "kind": "value-readout",
      "presentation": "Place compact comparison rows beneath the picture, followed by the bound status line. Arrows compare the starting nucleus with the explicitly named current scope. C counts chromosomes; k counts chromatids per chromosome; D counts DNA molecules. Joined sisters count as one chromosome until separation. Each chromatid contains one double-stranded DNA molecule. Compute D = C × k from the selected state; all counts are exact integers, without rounding.",
      "bind": {
        "values": "state.readouts"
      }
    }
  ],
  "controls": [
    {
      "id": "stage",
      "kind": "index",
      "items": "variant.states",
      "label": "Mitosis stage",
      "presentation": "Navigation uses Previous and Next, retaining those names when disabled at boundaries. Default: prophase; bounds: first through last state; increment: one state. The index selects biological states, never elapsed time. Every state persists until another learner action, including telophase. Parameter-control budget: zero, excluding navigation and Reset. Provide accessible names, visible focus, and keyboard operation."
    },
    {
      "id": "reset",
      "kind": "reset",
      "label": "Reset",
      "presentation": "Restore prophase and all defaults. Provide visible focus and keyboard operation. Reference captures must select and hold telophase."
    }
  ],
